.\"                                      Hey, EMACS: -*- nroff -*-
.TH DOCA\-HUGEPAGES 8 "2026-10-15"
.SH NAME
doca\-hugepages \- manage hugepage allocations for DOCA applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doca\-hugepages config
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.BI \-\-app " APP"
.BI \-\-size " SIZE_KB"
.BI \-\-num " NUM"
.PP
.B doca\-hugepages reload
.PP
.B doca\-hugepages remove
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.I APP
.PP
.B doca\-hugepages show
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doca\-hugepages
manages per\-application hugepage configurations stored in JSON files
under
.IR /etc/mellanox/hugepages.d/ .
Each application registers its hugepage requirements (page size and count);
the
.B reload
command then allocates the total hugepages needed across all registered
applications.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B config
Add or update the hugepage configuration for an application.
Requires
.BR \-\-app ", " \-\-size ", and " \-\-num .
Use
.B \-\-force
to skip the confirmation prompt when updating an existing entry.
This command only updates the stored configuration; use
.B reload
to apply changes.
.TP
.B reload
Read all per\-application configurations from
.I /etc/mellanox/hugepages.d/
and allocate the required hugepages via
.IR /sys/kernel/mm/hugepages/ .
.TP
.B remove
Remove the configuration for
.IR APP .
Use
.B \-\-all
to remove all size entries for the application without prompting.
.TP
.B show
Display the current hugepage configuration for all registered applications.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-app " APP"
Application name (arbitrary label, e.g.\& "ovs\-doca").
.TP
.BI \-\-size " SIZE_KB"
Hugepage size in kilobytes (e.g.\& 2048 for 2\ MB, 1048576 for 1\ GB).
Must be a size supported by the running kernel.
.TP
.BI \-\-num " NUM"
Number of hugepages to allocate for this application.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Skip the confirmation prompt when overwriting an existing configuration.
.TP
.B \-\-all
With
.BR remove ,
delete all size entries without prompting.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mellanox/hugepages.d/
Directory containing per\-application JSON configuration files.
Each file is named
.IB APP .json
and maps hugepage sizes to counts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mlnx\-bf\-hugepages (8),
.BR mlnx_bf_configure_ovs (8)
